@bennealon thanks for submitting this very useful post - I will look at it ASAP, probably after I come up with a solution for #25400. 

FWIW, I have 12 TRVs, but _no_ DHW - someone lets me use theirs, and maybe because I am afraid of leaving their HW off, I don't test it as well as I could.

When it comes to the time, maybe you might let me use yours?  You will have to provide access to me via the [evohome website](https://international.mytotalconnectcomfort.com/Account/Login) - PM me on https://community.home-assistant.io/ and I'll send you my email.

@zxdavb Hi David, updated HA to 0.99.0 and the above is still an issue 👎. If i ensure my evohome client is set to `off` and following scheduler - Changing to `on` through the UI forces a change to `off` AND the `preset` gets changed to now be `permanent`. So it appears to be making a communication to the evohome API, but just sending the wrong values.

The default action through the HA UI seems to be to set the `preset` to `permanent` (despite the UI not allowing me to change this), therefore the evohome API will be forced to no longer follow scheduler and therefore means i can never make a temporary change to the hot water system so that it eventually goes back to schedule.

Currently i am avoiding using this integration to control my DHW, and instead am using IFTTT triggers to get the functionality that i require 👍
